1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:06,698
Here there are two poles, one twelve feet and the other twenty-eight feet high, thirty feet apart.

2
00:00:06,648 --> 00:00:12,805
Each pole is held by a cable that runs down to the same stake driven into the ground between them.

3
00:00:12,805 --> 00:00:17,207
The variable x is the distance from the stake to the shorter pole.

4
00:00:17,207 --> 00:00:24,481
Drag the orange stake, move the slider or the point on the graph, and watch how the total length of cable changes.

5
00:00:24,481 --> 00:00:32,034
The endpoint button takes the stake to the foot of one of the poles, so you can compare the endpoints of the interval with the minimum.

6
00:00:32,034 --> 00:00:36,143
Notice also the angle that each cable makes with the ground.

7
00:00:36,143 --> 00:00:40,545
Then check your result with Go to optimum or with Reveal solution.

